help.en:
Leave-one-out cross-validation: each well is removed in turn, its value is predicted by kriging from the rest, and compared with the actual value. Helps tune the variogram (nugget, range, model) by error rather than by eye.

The Log reports metrics: ME (bias, → 0), RMSE (lower is better), MSDR (→ 1 means the variogram is adequate in scale), R. Try different parameters and compare RMSE and MSDR.

Residuals layer (opt.) - points with the following fields:
  • <well number> - if "Well number field" is set;
  • <validated field name> - the actual value;
  • z_est - kriging estimate from the other points (LOO);
  • error - estimate minus actual (minus: under, plus: over);
  • abs_error - absolute error;
  • std_resid - standardized residual: error / kriging standard error, signed (not a variance).
It shows where the model misses.

The HTML report (default) opens in the result viewer: an interactive "estimate vs actual" plot, an error histogram and a metrics table.

**Remove a polynomial trend** and **trend degree** repeat the parameters of the same name in 2D Kriging and are needed so that the check runs under the same conditions as the future computation. Checking a variogram without a trend and then building the grid with one means measuring the wrong thing.

**Save the profile under a name** records the checked set of parameters under the given name, and from then on it is applied in 2D Kriging by a single choice. An empty field means the profile is not saved and the result of the check stays in the report only.
